<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kokoda Track campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kokoda Track campaign was fought between July and November 1942 in the Owen Stanley Range of Papua, then an Australian territory. Japanese forces advancing overland towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-moresby">Port Moresby</a> were halted and pushed back by Australian troops, helped by Papuan carriers. The campaign became a defining episode in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s memory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kokoda-track-campaign.jpg" alt="Kokoda Track campaign" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Parer, Damien Peter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Australian_39th_Battalion_after_the_Kokoda_Track_campaign_1942_(AWM_013289).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
